6)
Step 1: Update the package list

sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
Step 2: Install Ansible

sudo apt install software-properties-common -y
sudo add-apt-repository --yes --update ppa:ansible/ansible
sudo apt install ansible -y
Step 3: Verify Ansible installation

ansible --version
Step 4: Create project directory

mkdir -p ~/ansible-apache
cd ~/ansible-apache
4. Ansible playbook
Create a file named apache.yml.

nano apache.yml
Add the following YAML content:

---
- name: Install Apache and Deploy Welcome Page
  hosts: localhost
  connection: local
  become: true

  tasks:
    - name: Update package cache and install Apache
      ansible.builtin.apt:
        name: apache2
        state: present
        update_cache: true

    - name: Start and enable Apache service
      ansible.builtin.service:
        name: apache2
        state: started
        enabled: true

    - name: Deploy welcome HTML page
      ansible.builtin.copy:
        dest: /var/www/html/index.html
        content: |
          <!DOCTYPE html>
          <html>
          <head>
              <title>Welcome Page</title>
          </head>
          <body>
              <h1>Welcome to My Web Application!</h1>
              <p>Apache web server deployed using Ansible.</p>
          </body>
          </html>
        mode: "0644"

    - name: Verify web application
      ansible.builtin.uri:
        url: http://127.0.0.1/
        status_code: 200

    - name: Display deployment status
      ansible.builtin.debug:
        msg: "Welcome web page deployed successfully!"
5. Implementation
Step 1: Execute the playbook

ansible-playbook apache.yml --ask-become-pass
Enter the sudo password when prompted.

Step 2: Verify Apache service

sudo systemctl status apache2
The service should show:

Active: active (running)
Step 3: Verify the web page

curl http://localhost
The HTML page should be returned.

Step 4: Open in browser

http://localhost
The welcome page should appear.

